{"id": "EUVD-2026-103005", "enisaUuid": "0e04f551-9aa5-3def-b2b9-553c70503b78", "description": "tarteaucitron.js before 1.37.0 contains a cross-site scripting vulnerability because getElemAttr resolves 'data-' prefixed attributes while the https-only guard validates the unprefixed attribute. Attackers who can place markup, such as CMS authors, can add data-url with a javascript: URL beside a benign url to execute script in the site's origin via iframe src.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:40:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T15:07:35", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AmauriC/tarteaucitron.js/commit/068653bd47f5d4a493251ca8e15bd2b0be9b544f", "https://github.com/AmauriC/tarteaucitron.js/releases/tag/v1.37.0", "https://github.com/AmauriC/tarteaucitron.js/blob/v1.36.0/tarteaucitron.js#L2641-L2648", "https://github.com/AmauriC/tarteaucitron.js/compare/v1.36.0...v1.37.0", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/tarteaucitron-js-before-1.37.0-xss-via-getelemattr-attribute-validation-mismatch"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111713", "GHSA-rfp9-xrhw-w637"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a5f37184-1471-3928-bbd6-3812f4f6dfac", "product": {"name": "tarteaucitron.js", "vendor": {"name": "amauric"}}, "product_version": "1.20.1 <1.37.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3fbdaeb5-1e54-3e79-bc9e-6d7423c19d26", "vendor": {"name": "amauric"}}], "isExploited": false}